IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- SCHEDULE 2: levy of Class 4 contributions with income tax (ssc8, layer 1).
-- Source: ukpga-1992-4.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from legislation.gov.uk
-- (point in time 2026-07-08). It is not the official text and nothing here is "verified against the
-- official text".
--
-- Paragraph numbers: the rendering drops them. The headings give paragraphs 1 (Interpretation, src:4748),
-- 2 (Method of computing profits or gains, 4755), 3 (Reliefs, 4759), 4 (Partnerships, 4787), 5 (Trustees, 4790) and
-- 6 (Other provisions, 4795); the sentence at src:4798 cites "paragraph 3(5) of this Schedule", which confirms 3.
-- The two paragraphs that follow with no heading are labelled 7 (src:4798) and 8 (src:4799) BY INFERENCE FROM THEIR POSITION:
-- see NOTES.md.
--
-- INPUTS: the Income Tax Acts' own tests ("relevant trade, profession or vocation", whether a loss arises from
-- activities whose profits would be brought into the computation, whether a payment is incurred wholly or
-- exclusively for the purposes of a trade, whether an assessment has become final) are facts the person or the
-- tax authority states; the rates and thresholds of Class 4 are section 15's, not this Schedule's.
-- Amounts are in pounds.

§ `Schedule 2 -- levy of Class 4 contributions with income tax`

§§ `Paragraph 1 -- interpretation`

-- The terms the paragraph defines, and a case for any other term.
DECLARE `sch 2 para 1 term` IS ONE OF
    `sch 2 para 1 the Act of 1988`
    `sch 2 para 1 ITTOIA 2005`
    `sch 2 para 1 ITA 2007`
    `sch 2 para 1 year`
    `sch 2 para 1 some other term`

-- src:4749 | In this Schedule—
-- src:4750 | (a) “the Act of 1988” means the Income and Corporation Taxes Act1988;
-- src:4751 | (ab) “ITTOIA 2005” means the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005;
-- src:4752 | (ac) “ITA 2007” means the Income Tax Act 2007;
-- src:4753 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:4754 | (c) “year” means year of assessment within the meaning of the Income Tax Acts (see section 989 of ITA 2007).
@ref sch 2 para 1 (src:4749-4754)
GIVEN term IS A `sch 2 para 1 term`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`sch 2 para 1 the meaning of the term` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `sch 2 para 1 the Act of 1988` THEN JUST "the Income and Corporation Taxes Act 1988"
    WHEN `sch 2 para 1 ITTOIA 2005` THEN JUST "the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005"
    WHEN `sch 2 para 1 ITA 2007` THEN JUST "the Income Tax Act 2007"
    WHEN `sch 2 para 1 year` THEN JUST "year of assessment within the meaning of the Income Tax Acts (see section 989 of ITA 2007)"
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the paragraph defines these four terms and no others
    WHEN `sch 2 para 1 some other term` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 2 -- method of computing profits or gains`

-- One profit or gain, with the facts the paragraph asks about it.
DECLARE `sch 2 a profit` HAS
    `the amount of the profit in pounds`                                                    IS A NUMBER
    `it is a profit of a relevant trade, profession or vocation`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trade, profession or vocation is carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of ITTOIA 2005`               IS A BOOLEAN

-- "Subject to the following paragraphs, Class 4 contributions shall be payable in respect of the full amount of all profits (a) ... and (b) ...".
-- src:4756 | Subject to the following paragraphs, Class 4 contributions shall be payable in respect of the full amount of all profits—
-- src:4757 | (a) which are the profits of any relevant trade, profession or vocation which is not carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom, and
-- src:4758 | (b) which are chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of ITTOIA 2005.
@ref sch 2 para 2 (src:4756-4758)
GIVEN profit IS A `sch 2 a profit`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 para 2 the profit is one in respect of which Class 4 contributions are payable` MEANS
    IF profit's `it is a profit of a relevant trade, profession or vocation`
       AND (NOT profit's `the trade, profession or vocation is carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom`)
       AND profit's `it is chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of ITTOIA 2005`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph says what is payable on profits (a) and (b) and nothing of any other profit
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The full amount of all such profits: the sum of the amounts of the profits that meet both limbs.
-- src:4756 | Subject to the following paragraphs, Class 4 contributions shall be payable in respect of the full amount of all profits—
-- src:4757 | (a) which are the profits of any relevant trade, profession or vocation which is not carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom, and
-- src:4758 | (b) which are chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of ITTOIA 2005.
@ref sch 2 para 2 (src:4756-4758)
GIVEN profits IS A LIST OF `sch 2 a profit`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 2 para 2 the full amount of the profits in respect of which Class 4 contributions are payable` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN p YIELD p's `the amount of the profit in pounds`)
             (filter (GIVEN p YIELD `sch 2 para 2 the profit is one in respect of which Class 4 contributions are payable` p EQUALS JUST TRUE)
                     profits))

§§ `Paragraph 3 -- reliefs`

-- The relief provisions that sub-paragraphs (1) and (2) name.
DECLARE `sch 2 para 3 relief provision` IS ONE OF
    `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 sections 64 and 72`
    `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 section 83`
    `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 section 89`
    `sch 2 para 3 Act of 1988 Chapter I of Part VII`
    `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 Chapters 2 and 3 of Part 3`
    `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 sections 457, 458 and 459`
    `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 section 383`
    `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 sections 88 and 94`
    `sch 2 para 3 sections 619 and 620`
    `sch 2 para 3 section 639`
    `sch 2 para 3 some other provision`

-- (1): "relief shall be available under, and in the manner provided by, the following provisions of ITA 2007".
-- src:4760 | (1) For the purposes of computing the amount of profits ... in respect of which Class 4 contributions are payable, relief shall be available under, and in the manner provided by, the following provisions of ITA 2007—
-- src:4761 | (a) sections 64 and 72 (set-off of trade losses against general income), but only where loss arises from activities the profits ... of which would be brought into computation for the purposes of Class 4 contributions;
-- src:4762 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:4763 | (c) section 83 (carry-forward of loss against subsequent profits); and
-- src:4764 | (d) section 89 (carry-back of terminal losses).
@ref sch 2 para 3(1) (src:4760-4764)
GIVEN provision IS A `sch 2 para 3 relief provision`
      `the loss arises from activities the profits of which would be brought into computation for the purposes of Class 4 contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 para 3(1) relief is available under the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 sections 64 and 72` THEN
        IF `the loss arises from activities the profits of which would be brought into computation for the purposes of Class 4 contributions`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but only where loss arises from activities the profits ... of which would be brought into computation for the purposes of Class 4 contributions"
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 section 83` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 section 89` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): sub-paragraph (1) lists the provisions under which relief is available and does not close the list
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 Act of 1988 Chapter I of Part VII` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 Chapters 2 and 3 of Part 3` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 sections 457, 458 and 459` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 section 383` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 sections 88 and 94` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 sections 619 and 620` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 section 639` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 some other provision` THEN NOTHING

-- (2): "The following relief provisions ... shall not apply".
-- src:4765 | (2) The following relief provisions ... shall not apply, that is to say—
-- src:4766 | (a) Chapter I of Part VII of the Act of 1988 and Chapters 2 and 3 of Part 3 and sections 457, 458 and 459 of ITA 2007 (personal reliefs);
-- src:4767 | (b) section 383 of ITA 2007 (relief for payment of interest);
-- src:4768 | (c) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:4769 | (d) sections 88 and 94 of ITA 2007 (treatment of interest as a loss for purposes of carry-forward or carry-back);
-- src:4770 | (e) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . ...
-- src:4771 | (f) sections 619 and 620 (premiums or other consideration under annuity contracts and trust schemes); and
-- src:4772 | (g) section 639 (personal pension contributions).
@ref sch 2 para 3(2) (src:4765-4772)
GIVEN provision IS A `sch 2 para 3 relief provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 para 3(2) the relief provision does not apply` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    -- the flat negative: the provision is named, so the text says it does not apply
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 Act of 1988 Chapter I of Part VII` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 Chapters 2 and 3 of Part 3` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 sections 457, 458 and 459` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 section 383` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 sections 88 and 94` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 sections 619 and 620` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 section 639` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): sub-paragraph (2) names the provisions that do not apply and does not close the list
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 sections 64 and 72` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 section 83` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 ITA 2007 section 89` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `sch 2 para 3 some other provision` THEN NOTHING

-- One year of a carry-forward: the profits for the year and the new amount to be deducted that arises in it.
DECLARE `sch 2 para 3 a year` HAS
    `the profits for the year in pounds`                 IS A NUMBER
    `the new amount to deduct that arises in the year`   IS A NUMBER

-- How much of what is waiting is absorbed in the year: "as far as may be", so no more than the profits.
GIVEN carried IS A NUMBER
      year IS A `sch 2 para 3 a year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 2 para 3(4) and (5) the amount absorbed in the year` MEANS
    min (carried PLUS year's `the new amount to deduct that arises in the year`)
        (max 0 (year's `the profits for the year in pounds`))

-- What is carried on to the next year after this one.
GIVEN carried IS A NUMBER
      year IS A `sch 2 para 3 a year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 2 para 3(4) and (5) the amount carried on from the year` MEANS
    (carried PLUS year's `the new amount to deduct that arises in the year`)
        MINUS `sch 2 para 3(4) and (5) the amount absorbed in the year` carried year

-- The profits for each year after the deduction, the excess going "from those of the immediately following year,
-- and, so far as it cannot be so deducted, then from those of the next year, and so on".
GIVEN carried IS A NUMBER
      years IS A LIST OF `sch 2 para 3 a year`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`sch 2 para 3(4) and (5) the profits for each year after the deduction` MEANS
    CONSIDER years
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN year FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (year's `the profits for the year in pounds` MINUS `sch 2 para 3(4) and (5) the amount absorbed in the year` carried year)
        FOLLOWED BY
        (`sch 2 para 3(4) and (5) the profits for each year after the deduction`
            (`sch 2 para 3(4) and (5) the amount carried on from the year` carried year) rest)

-- What is still waiting after the last year given.
GIVEN carried IS A NUMBER
      years IS A LIST OF `sch 2 para 3 a year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 2 para 3(4) and (5) the amount still to be deducted after the last year` MEANS
    CONSIDER years
    WHEN EMPTY THEN carried
    WHEN year FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        `sch 2 para 3(4) and (5) the amount still to be deducted after the last year`
            (`sch 2 para 3(4) and (5) the amount carried on from the year` carried year) rest

-- (4): a loss deduction in a year from 1990-91 for which the person claims and is allowed relief under (1).
-- src:4774 | (4) Where in the year 1990-1991 or any subsequent year of assessment for which a person claims and is allowed relief by virtue of sub-paragraph (1) above there falls to be made in computing his net income for income tax purposes a deduction in respect of any loss in any relevant trade, profession or vocation—
-- src:4775 | (a) the amount of the deduction shall, as far as may be, be treated for the purpose of the charge to Class 4 contributions as reducing the person’s profits ... for that year of any relevant trade, profession or vocation, and
-- src:4776 | (b) any excess shall be treated for that purpose as reducing such profits ... for subsequent years (being deducted as far as may be from those of the immediately following year, whether or not the person claims or is entitled to claim relief under this paragraph for that year, and, so far as it cannot be so deducted, then from those of the next year, and so on).
@ref sch 2 para 3(4) (src:4774-4776)
GIVEN `the person claims and is allowed relief by virtue of sub-paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the year of the deduction` IS A `Tax year`
      `the deduction in respect of the loss` IS A NUMBER
      `the profits for that year and for each following year` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF NUMBER)
`sch 2 para 3(4) the profits for each year after the loss is deducted` MEANS
    IF `the person claims and is allowed relief by virtue of sub-paragraph (1)`
       AND `the year of the deduction`'s `calendar year in which it begins` AT LEAST 1990
    THEN JUST (`sch 2 para 3(4) and (5) the profits for each year after the deduction` `the deduction in respect of the loss`
                  (map (GIVEN p YIELD (`sch 2 para 3 a year` OF p, 0)) `the profits for that year and for each following year`))
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): sub-paragraph (4) is for "the year 1990-1991 or any subsequent year of assessment for which a person claims and is allowed relief"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4774 | (4) Where in the year 1990-1991 or any subsequent year of assessment for which a person claims and is allowed relief by virtue of sub-paragraph (1) above there falls to be made in computing his net income for income tax purposes a deduction in respect of any loss in any relevant trade, profession or vocation—
-- src:4775 | (a) the amount of the deduction shall, as far as may be, be treated for the purpose of the charge to Class 4 contributions as reducing the person’s profits ... for that year of any relevant trade, profession or vocation, and
-- src:4776 | (b) any excess shall be treated for that purpose as reducing such profits ... for subsequent years (being deducted as far as may be from those of the immediately following year, whether or not the person claims or is entitled to claim relief under this paragraph for that year, and, so far as it cannot be so deducted, then from those of the next year, and so on).
@ref sch 2 para 3(4) (src:4774-4776)
GIVEN `the deduction in respect of the loss` IS A NUMBER
      `the profits for that year and for each following year` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 2 para 3(4) the excess still to be deducted after the last year given` MEANS
    `sch 2 para 3(4) and (5) the amount still to be deducted after the last year`
        `the deduction in respect of the loss`
        (map (GIVEN p YIELD (`sch 2 para 3 a year` OF p, 0)) `the profits for that year and for each following year`)

-- (5): the payments that are relieved, and what each is made of.
DECLARE `sch 2 para 3(5) kind of payment` IS ONE OF
    `sch 2 para 3(5)(b) a payment under section 383 of ITA 2007`
    `sch 2 para 3(5)(c) a payment from which tax must be deducted under section 900(2), 903(5) or 906(5) of ITA 2007`
    `sch 2 para 3(5)(d) a payment from which tax must be deducted under section 910(2) of ITA 2007`
    `sch 2 para 3(5)(e) a payment from which tax must be deducted as a result of a direction under section 944(2) of ITA 2007`
    `sch 2 para 3(5) some other payment`

DECLARE `sch 2 para 3(5) a payment` HAS
    `the kind of payment`                                                    IS A `sch 2 para 3(5) kind of payment`
    `the amount of the payment in pounds`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `the chargeable amount referred to in section 910(2) of ITA 2007`        IS A NUMBER
    `relief from income tax is or can be given for it`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is incurred wholly or exclusively for the purposes of a relevant trade, profession or vocation` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:4777 | (5) Relief shall be allowed, in respect of—
-- src:4778 | (a) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:4779 | (b) payments under section 383 of ITA 2007 (relief for payment of interest), being payments for which relief from income tax is or can be given,
-- src:4780 | (c) payments from which a sum representing income tax must be deducted under—
-- src:4781 | (i) section 900(2) of ITA 2007 (commercial payments made by individuals),
-- src:4782 | (ii) section 903(5) of that Act (patent royalties), or
-- src:4783 | (iii) section 906(5) of that Act (certain royalties etc where usual place of abode of owner is abroad),
-- src:4784 | (d) so much of any payment from which a sum representing income tax must be deducted under section 910(2) of ITA 2007 (proceeds of a sale of patent rights: payments to non-UK residents) as is equal to the amount referred to in that provision as “the chargeable amount”, or
-- src:4785 | (e) a payment from which a sum representing income tax must be deducted as a result of a direction under section 944(2) of ITA 2007 (tax avoidance: certain payments to non-UK residents)
-- src:4786 | so far as the payment is incurred wholly or exclusively for the purposes of any relevant trade, profession or vocation, by way of deduction from or set-off against profits ... chargeable to Class 4 contributions for the year in which the payments are made; and, in the case of any insufficiency of the profits ... of that year, the payments shall be carried forward and deducted from or set off against the profits ... of any subsequent year (being deducted or set off as far as may be from or against the profits ... of the immediately following year, whether or not relief can be claimed under this paragraph for that year, and so far as it cannot be so deducted, from or against those of the next year, and so on).
@ref sch 2 para 3(5) (src:4777-4786)
GIVEN payment IS A `sch 2 para 3(5) a payment`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 2 para 3(5) the amount of the payment for which relief is allowed` MEANS
    IF payment's `it is incurred wholly or exclusively for the purposes of a relevant trade, profession or vocation`
    THEN
        CONSIDER payment's `the kind of payment`
        WHEN `sch 2 para 3(5)(b) a payment under section 383 of ITA 2007` THEN
            IF payment's `relief from income tax is or can be given for it`
            THEN JUST (payment's `the amount of the payment in pounds`)
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "being payments for which relief from income tax is or can be given"
            ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `sch 2 para 3(5)(c) a payment from which tax must be deducted under section 900(2), 903(5) or 906(5) of ITA 2007` THEN
            JUST (payment's `the amount of the payment in pounds`)
        -- only "so much of any payment ... as is equal to the amount referred to in that provision as 'the chargeable amount'"
        WHEN `sch 2 para 3(5)(d) a payment from which tax must be deducted under section 910(2) of ITA 2007` THEN
            JUST (payment's `the chargeable amount referred to in section 910(2) of ITA 2007`)
        WHEN `sch 2 para 3(5)(e) a payment from which tax must be deducted as a result of a direction under section 944(2) of ITA 2007` THEN
            JUST (payment's `the amount of the payment in pounds`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): sub-paragraph (5) lists the payments relieved and does not close the list
        WHEN `sch 2 para 3(5) some other payment` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "so far as the payment is incurred wholly or exclusively for the purposes of any relevant trade, profession or vocation"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (5): the profits for each year after the relieved payments are deducted, the shortfall carried forward in the same way as in (4).
-- src:4786 | so far as the payment is incurred wholly or exclusively for the purposes of any relevant trade, profession or vocation, by way of deduction from or set-off against profits ... chargeable to Class 4 contributions for the year in which the payments are made; and, in the case of any insufficiency of the profits ... of that year, the payments shall be carried forward and deducted from or set off against the profits ... of any subsequent year (being deducted or set off as far as may be from or against the profits ... of the immediately following year, whether or not relief can be claimed under this paragraph for that year, and so far as it cannot be so deducted, from or against those of the next year, and so on).
@ref sch 2 para 3(5) (src:4786)
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `sch 2 para 3 a year`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`sch 2 para 3(5) the profits for each year after the payments are deducted` MEANS
    `sch 2 para 3(4) and (5) the profits for each year after the deduction` 0 years

-- src:4786 | so far as the payment is incurred wholly or exclusively for the purposes of any relevant trade, profession or vocation, by way of deduction from or set-off against profits ... chargeable to Class 4 contributions for the year in which the payments are made; and, in the case of any insufficiency of the profits ... of that year, the payments shall be carried forward and deducted from or set off against the profits ... of any subsequent year (being deducted or set off as far as may be from or against the profits ... of the immediately following year, whether or not relief can be claimed under this paragraph for that year, and so far as it cannot be so deducted, from or against those of the next year, and so on).
@ref sch 2 para 3(5) (src:4786)
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `sch 2 para 3 a year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 2 para 3(5) the payments still to be deducted after the last year given` MEANS
    `sch 2 para 3(4) and (5) the amount still to be deducted after the last year` 0 years

§§ `Paragraph 4 -- partnerships`

-- One share of profits or gains.
DECLARE `sch 2 para 4 a share` HAS
    `the amount of the share in pounds`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `it is immediately derived by the person from carrying on the trade, profession or vocation` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (1): liability arises in respect of his share, aggregated with his share of the profits of any other trade, profession or vocation,
-- "so far as immediately derived by him".
-- src:4788 | (1) Where a trade or profession is carried on by two or more persons jointly, the liability of any one of them in respect of Class 4 contributions shall arise in respect of his share of the profits ... of that trade or profession (so far as immediately derived by him from carrying it on); and for this purpose his share shall be aggregated with his share of the profits ... of any other trade, profession or vocation (so far as immediately derived by him from carrying it on or exercising it).
@ref sch 2 para 4(1) (src:4788)
GIVEN `the trade or profession is carried on by two or more persons jointly` IS A BOOLEAN
      shares IS A LIST OF `sch 2 para 4 a share`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 2 para 4(1) the profits in respect of which the partner's liability arises` MEANS
    IF `the trade or profession is carried on by two or more persons jointly`
    THEN JUST (sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD s's `the amount of the share in pounds`)
                        (filter (GIVEN s YIELD s's `it is immediately derived by the person from carrying on the trade, profession or vocation`) shares)))
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a trade or profession is carried on by two or more persons jointly"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (2): "shall be charged on him separately".
-- src:4789 | (2) Where sub-paragraph (1) above applies, the Class 4 contributions for which a person is liable in respect of the profits ... of the trade or profession carried on jointly (aggregated, where appropriate, as mentioned in that sub-paragraph) shall be charged on him separately.
@ref sch 2 para 4(2) (src:4789)
GIVEN `sub-paragraph (1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 para 4(2) the contributions are charged on the partner separately` MEANS
    IF `sub-paragraph (1) applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where sub-paragraph (1) above applies"
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 5 -- trustees, etc.`

-- "such contributions shall not be payable either by him or by any other person" (paragraph (a) is shown blank in this text).
-- src:4791 | In any circumstances in which apart from this paragraph a person would—
-- src:4792 | (a) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:4793 | (b) by virtue of section 8 of ITTOIA 2005 be assessed and charged to Class 4 contributions in respect of profits ... received or receivable by him in the capacity of trustee,
-- src:4794 | such contributions shall not be payable either by him or by any other person.
@ref sch 2 para 5 (src:4791-4794)
GIVEN `a person would, apart from this paragraph, be assessed and charged to Class 4 contributions by virtue of section 8 of ITTOIA 2005 in respect of profits received or receivable by them as trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 para 5 Class 4 contributions are payable on the profits received as trustee` MEANS
    IF `a person would, apart from this paragraph, be assessed and charged to Class 4 contributions by virtue of section 8 of ITTOIA 2005 in respect of profits received or receivable by them as trustee`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "such contributions shall not be payable either by him or by any other person"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any circumstances in which apart from this paragraph a person would ... be assessed and charged ... in the capacity of trustee"
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 6 -- other provisions`

DECLARE `sch 2 para 6(1) kind of sum` IS ONE OF
    `sch 2 para 6(1) an amount due in respect of Class 4 contributions`
    `sch 2 para 6(1) a sum to be paid by Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs in respect of Class 4 contributions`
    `sch 2 para 6(1) some other sum`

-- (1), first limb: section 101 of the Finance Act 2009 (late payment interest) applies to any amount due in respect of Class 4 contributions.
-- src:4796 | (1) Section 101 of the Finance Act 2009 (late payment interest on sums due to HMRC) shall apply in relation to any amount due in respect of Class 4 contributions as it applies in relation to income tax; and section 102 of the Finance Act 2009 (repayment interest on sums to be paid by HMRC) shall, with the necessary modifications, apply in relation to Class 4 contributions as it applies in relation to income tax.
@ref sch 2 para 6(1) (src:4796)
GIVEN sum IS A `sch 2 para 6(1) kind of sum`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 para 6(1) section 101 of the Finance Act 2009 applies to the sum` MEANS
    CONSIDER sum
    WHEN `sch 2 para 6(1) an amount due in respect of Class 4 contributions` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the first limb is "any amount due in respect of Class 4 contributions"
    WHEN `sch 2 para 6(1) a sum to be paid by Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs in respect of Class 4 contributions` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `sch 2 para 6(1) some other sum` THEN NOTHING

-- (1), second limb: section 102 (repayment interest) applies, with the necessary modifications, to sums to be paid by HMRC.
-- src:4796 | (1) Section 101 of the Finance Act 2009 (late payment interest on sums due to HMRC) shall apply in relation to any amount due in respect of Class 4 contributions as it applies in relation to income tax; and section 102 of the Finance Act 2009 (repayment interest on sums to be paid by HMRC) shall, with the necessary modifications, apply in relation to Class 4 contributions as it applies in relation to income tax.
@ref sch 2 para 6(1) (src:4796)
GIVEN sum IS A `sch 2 para 6(1) kind of sum`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 para 6(1) section 102 of the Finance Act 2009 applies to the sum` MEANS
    CONSIDER sum
    WHEN `sch 2 para 6(1) a sum to be paid by Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs in respect of Class 4 contributions` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the second limb is "sums to be paid by HMRC" in relation to Class 4 contributions
    WHEN `sch 2 para 6(1) an amount due in respect of Class 4 contributions` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `sch 2 para 6(1) some other sum` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 7 -- final assessments (label inferred)`

-- First limb: "Where an assessment has become final and conclusive for the purposes of income tax for any year, that assessment
-- shall also be final and conclusive for the purposes of computing liability for Class 4 contributions".
-- src:4798 | Where an assessment has become final and conclusive for the purposes of income tax for any year, that assessment shall also be final and conclusive for the purposes of computing liability for Class 4 contributions; and no allowance or adjustment of liability, on the ground of diminution of income or loss, shall be taken into account in computing profits ... chargeable to Class 4 contributions unless that allowance or adjustment has previously been made on an application under the special provisions of the Income Tax Acts relating to it, or falls to be allowed under paragraph 3(5) of this Schedule.
@ref sch 2 para 7 (src:4798)
GIVEN `the assessment has become final and conclusive for the purposes of income tax for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 para 7 the assessment is final and conclusive for computing Class 4 liability` MEANS
    IF `the assessment has become final and conclusive for the purposes of income tax for the year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an assessment has become final and conclusive for the purposes of income tax"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Second limb: "no allowance or adjustment of liability, on the ground of diminution of income or loss, shall be taken into account in
-- computing profits ... unless that allowance or adjustment has previously been made on an application under the special provisions
-- of the Income Tax Acts relating to it, or falls to be allowed under paragraph 3(5) of this Schedule".
-- src:4798 | Where an assessment has become final and conclusive for the purposes of income tax for any year, that assessment shall also be final and conclusive for the purposes of computing liability for Class 4 contributions; and no allowance or adjustment of liability, on the ground of diminution of income or loss, shall be taken into account in computing profits ... chargeable to Class 4 contributions unless that allowance or adjustment has previously been made on an application under the special provisions of the Income Tax Acts relating to it, or falls to be allowed under paragraph 3(5) of this Schedule.
@ref sch 2 para 7 (src:4798)
GIVEN `the allowance or adjustment has previously been made on an application under the special provisions of the Income Tax Acts relating to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allowance or adjustment falls to be allowed under paragraph 3(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 para 7 the allowance or adjustment may be taken into account in computing the profits` MEANS
    IF `the allowance or adjustment has previously been made on an application under the special provisions of the Income Tax Acts relating to it`
       OR `the allowance or adjustment falls to be allowed under paragraph 3(5)`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception ends the bar; the sentence does not itself grant the allowance
    THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no allowance or adjustment of liability, on the ground of diminution of income or loss, shall be taken into account ... unless"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Paragraph 8 -- appeals (label inferred)`

DECLARE `sch 2 para 8 kind of matter` IS ONE OF
    `sch 2 para 8 an appeal or other matter under Part V of the Taxes Management Act 1970 in relation to Class 4 contributions`
    `sch 2 para 8 a decision under section 17(1) whether a person is excepted from liability for Class 4 contributions or the liability is deferred`
    `sch 2 para 8 a decision under regulations made by virtue of section 17(3) or (4) or 18`
    `sch 2 para 8 some other matter`

-- src:4799 | The provisions of Part V of the Taxes Management Act 1970 (appeals, etc.) shall apply with the necessary modifications in relation to Class 4 contributions as they apply in relation to income tax; but nothing in this Schedule affects the extent to which the Income Tax Acts apply with respect to any decision falling to be made—
-- src:4800 | (a) under subsection (1) of section 17 above or subsection (1) of section 17 of the Northern Ireland Contributions and Benefits Act as to whether by regulations under that subsection a person is excepted from liability for Class 4 contributions, or his liability is deferred; or
-- src:4801 | (b) under regulations made by virtue of section 17(3) or (4) or 18 above or section 17(3) or (4) or 18 of the Northern Ireland Contributions and Benefits Act.
@ref sch 2 para 8 (src:4799-4801)
GIVEN matter IS A `sch 2 para 8 kind of matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 para 8 Part V of the Taxes Management Act 1970 applies to the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `sch 2 para 8 an appeal or other matter under Part V of the Taxes Management Act 1970 in relation to Class 4 contributions` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "nothing in this Schedule affects the extent to which the Income Tax Acts apply with respect to any decision falling to be made" under these provisions
    WHEN `sch 2 para 8 a decision under section 17(1) whether a person is excepted from liability for Class 4 contributions or the liability is deferred` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `sch 2 para 8 a decision under regulations made by virtue of section 17(3) or (4) or 18` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says nothing of any other matter
    WHEN `sch 2 para 8 some other matter` THEN NOTHING
